# PART 2 — UNDERSTAND THE PRODUCT BEFORE CODING

## 2.1 The actual product

FairResolve is an evidence-aware, policy-grounded customer dispute investigation and refund resolution platform for small and medium-sized online merchants who use PayPal.

Its purpose is to transform an unstructured customer complaint into a structured investigation, evaluate it against the merchant's refund policy and help the merchant make a defensible resolution decision.

When the merchant explicitly authorizes an eligible refund, FairResolve executes that refund through PayPal.

### Official product description

FairResolve turns an unstructured customer complaint into a structured, evidence-aware, policy-grounded resolution, then lets the merchant approve and execute that resolution through PayPal.

This is not another AI chatbot.

It is an operational dispute-investigation product with a real payment integration.

## 2.2 The problem we are solving

Online merchants receive complaints such as:

- "My product arrived damaged."
- "I received a different product."
- "My order was delivered to the wrong address."
- "I never received my parcel."
- "The product doesn't match the description."
- "I want my money back."

A normal support workflow requires a person to locate the order, read the complaint, inspect available evidence, consult the return policy, decide what information is missing, calculate the appropriate refund and execute the payment action.

This process can be slow, inconsistent and expensive for small businesses.

FairResolve should reduce manual work without pretending that AI can determine whether every customer is telling the truth.

## 2.3 The most important product principle

**A customer's claim is not a verified fact. An AI observation is not proof. A recommendation is not authorization.**

The system must explicitly distinguish:

1. Customer-reported information.
2. Merchant-provided information.
3. PayPal-verified transaction information.
4. Carrier-verified information, only when a real carrier integration exists.
5. Evidence received from the customer.
6. AI-generated observations about evidence.
7. Deterministic policy-engine results.
8. The merchant's final decision.
9. The actual PayPal refund result.

Never combine all these categories into one supposedly verified AI answer.

FairResolve must communicate uncertainty honestly.

## 2.4 First target customers

Focus the initial product on:

**Small and medium-sized online merchants using PayPal who do not have a dedicated refund investigation or customer-support engineering team.**

Do not attempt to build a complete enterprise CRM, full chargeback-management platform or universal fraud-detection system.

The first release must deliver one complete, reliable workflow exceptionally well.

