# PART 15 — FAILURE HANDLING AND RELIABILITY

The application should remain usable when external services fail.

### AI provider failure

- Save the complaint.
- Mark the investigation as incomplete or failed.
- Display a meaningful message.
- Allow manual review.
- Retry only within bounded rules.
- Never leave the case loading indefinitely.

### PayPal failure

- Preserve the approval and refund-attempt history.
- Record the real error category safely.
- Do not claim that the refund succeeded.
- Reconcile ambiguous outcomes.
- Allow a safe recovery action.

### Database failure

- Return a controlled service error.
- Do not return raw stack traces.
- Do not silently acknowledge a write that was not committed.

### Evidence-processing failure

- Quarantine the upload.
- Explain the problem.
- Allow a safe re-upload.
- Never pass an unvalidated file to the AI provider.

### Worker failure

- Record job attempts.
- Recover eligible stale jobs.
- Use bounded backoff.
- Keep jobs idempotent.
- Expose operational status to administrators.

### Frontend failure

- Provide useful error boundaries.
- Prevent repeated accidental submission.
- Preserve user-entered information where safe.
- Never mark an action successful based only on the button click.

